# What never enters the build context.
#
# This is not only a size list. `COPY . .` in the build stage would otherwise
# pull .env — which holds ARGUS_KEY — into an image layer. The runtime stage
# copies only dist/ and dist-server/, so it would not reach the published image,
# but the build stage is still a layer that can be tagged, cached and pushed.
# Keep the secret out of the context entirely rather than relying on which stage
# gets published.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Rights-encumbered media, excluded for the same reason .gitignore excludes it
# and with the same reasoning: shipping it should be impossible by default
# rather than dependent on someone remembering.
#
# These are gitignored, so a CI build checking the repo out never sees them --
# but a `docker build` on the machine that owns the files does, and Vite copies
# public/ into dist/ verbatim. Without these two lines a local build bakes a
# commercial release into an image and a push publishes it. Verified: they were
# in the image before this was added.
#
# If you have swapped in a track and artwork you own, delete these two lines.
#
# Note the `**/`. Unlike .gitignore, .dockerignore matches with Go's
# filepath.Match, where `*` does not cross a path separator: a bare `*.mp3`
# matches only the context root and silently leaves public/track.mp3 in the
# build. That exact mistake was made here first and caught by listing the image.
**/*.mp3
public/cover.webp

# Bulk that has no business in a build. The .blend files are ~6.5 MB each and
# the tools venv holds bpy at ~357 MB; neither is used to build the site, since
# public/room.glb is committed already built.
*.blend
*.blend1
tools/.venv/
tools/shots/
tools/preview/

# Rebuilt inside the image, so copying them in would only risk a stale or
# host-arch-specific result being reused.
node_modules/
dist/
dist-server/
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

.git/
.github/
helm/
.gitignore
.dockerignore
Dockerfile
*.md
.DS_Store
*.local
